From a74ddb60c1679ac35ced98f45ad41f6385d77910 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 11:09:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] feat(email-intelligence): smart links, attachment
 detection, insights panel

All client-side heuristics over data already returned by the existing
/emails/:id endpoint - no new API routes, no new Gemini calls, no API
contract changes.

- detectLinks(): finds URLs and categorizes known providers (Zoom,
  Google Meet, Microsoft Teams, Google Forms, Docs, Drive, GitHub,
  Notion, Figma, Jira, Trello, LeetCode, Codeforces) into a provider +
  action label; unknown URLs still come back with a generic 'Open Link'
  label rather than being dropped.
- detectAttachments(): finds filename-like mentions (Assignment.pdf,
  Report.docx, Poster.png, etc.) and pairs them with a URL only if one
  actually appears on the same line - never fabricates a download link
  that doesn't exist. Unlinked mentions show 'Mentioned in email'
  instead of a broken button.
- detectDeadlines(): resolves 'today', 'tomorrow', weekday names (with
  optional 'next'), 'next week', and month-day dates (full or
  abbreviated, e.g. 'Aug 5') to real dates relative to the email's
  receivedAt; bare time mentions ('before 5 PM') are kept as unresolved
  time constraints rather than guessed at.
- computeInsights(): reading time, urgency (keyword + existing priority
  field), requires-reply, and boolean flags for deadline/attachment/
  meeting/payment/form/external-link/contact-info - all derived, none
  invented.

New components render these on the email details page: SmartLinks
(branded action buttons), AttachmentList (icon + Download/Preview or
'Mentioned in email'), EmailInsights (reading time, urgency, requires-
reply, insight chips, detected deadlines). Each renders nothing when
there's nothing to show, so empty emails don't get empty boxes.

Fixed during testing: the initial attachment filename regex allowed
spaces/dots in the base name and would swallow multiple real filenames
plus the prose between them into one bogus match - tightened to not
cross word/space boundaries; verified against a multi-attachment,
multi-link sample email.
